[Minor spoilers all around, be warned]



You may realize that this happens differently for different
potions/scrolls. An extra-healing potion is very clear in its effect, and
you know/ID it once you've seen it used. Others are less clear ("You
feel threatened"? huh?) so you recognize that something happened but
aren't sure what - then finding another potion/scroll named "potion1" (or
"threatened" if named after the fact), you can study the effects more
carefully.

The point being: the game is consistent, and these things will make sense
once you get the overall hang of it. Just keep playing with your eyes
open, and don't be afraid to experiment.

> And here are my questions of the day:
> 
> 1. What is riding good for?

Heh, less tiresome to move about. ;-)
Seriously, it's really cool if you exercise it, and potential for many
interesting things (imagine riding a flying steed to avoid falling into a
poisoned pit, for instance). Unless you're really into it, though, I'd
recommend you master the game on foot first. ;-)

> 2. Why is some armor not automatically identified when put on, and
> some is?! Quite random...

Ah, some armour is easier to recognize than others. A chain mail is a
chain mail is a chain mail, but this ornamental cape over there may have
some non-obvious magical properties. Rule of thumb: you'll immediately
identify "obvious" things (like chests), but some things including
armour and weapons have their descriptions randomized every game; you can
normally assume that these random ones are either magical or mixed in to
make it harder for you to identify magical items. Yes, it's a cruel game.

Incidentally, you probably figured out that wearing any armour immediately
identifies its enchantment (+/-), and that "fighter" classes are better at
identifying non-random armour.


> 4. In the status area, my strenght was indicated 18/02. What does this
> mean?

"Normal" strength goes up to 18. After that, it's gained in (sort of) 0.01
increments. You have about 18.02 strength. If you keep getting stronger,
you'll make it to 18.99, then to 18.**, which is pretty much the
non-magical limit (depending also on race/class). It can be further
enhanced beyond that by magical means.

> 5. What is the difference between wearing and eating rings?

Similar to having your cake and eating it? 8-)
Many rings, when eaten, have a chance of conferring the magic they
contain. Thus, if you eat a ring of searching you may (or may not) get
intrinsic searching, freeing up a finger.
[This is the tip of the proverbial iceberg, lots of circumstantial advice
applies; experiment]


> 6. How does one use identify scrolls properly? Some can identify more
> than one item when read, but it is impossible to set the
> order/priority of the object I want to identify

Yeah, the interface design is nonintuitive. Just select one item, and if
the scroll would have identified an additional object, it will prompt you
again.


> 7. Why am I sometimes asked "Really attack the XYZ-Monster?"? And
> sometimes I am not promted, eventhough it's the same type of monster.
> Quite random...

Try looking (';') at the monster next time it asks you. This gnome here
may prompt the prompt, while the one over there won't, because they have a
fundamental philosophical difference about your presence in their dungeon.


> 8. Sometime I see "peaceful watchmen". Suddenly if I break open a door
> nearby, he becomes hostile (and these guys, especially the watch
> captains are very deadly), even if there is nothing in the room!?

Where you live, cops don't get mad if you break open someone else's empty
room? They want you to behave, breaking doors ain't behavin'. It's OK, as
long as you can persuade them to see things your way, with liberal
application of deadly force. Or leave the doors (and fountains!) alone
until you can.


> 9. What is this story about "luck" (eg. you were unlucky/very
> unlucky/luck/etc.)?

Lady luck is a fickle mistress, but luck in nethack is measurable and
affects a large number of things. Check the guidebook or ask the Oracle if
you want to deduce it, or look at the spoilers for the exhaustive details.

The short version, how lucky you are affects pretty much everything you
do. So try to stay as lucky as possible.

Good luck. ;-)

